finding: P2: OptionOf drops the absent/default case for optional properties. EntryFor<{type:"texture"; dimension?:"2d-array"}>["texture"] is only WgslTexture2dArray<F32>, but bindingEntry of {type:"texture"} returns texture_2d. EntryFor<{type:"sampler"; samplerType?:"comparison"}>["sampler"] is only "comparison", but bindingEntry of {type:"sampler"} returns "filtering". Both are valid MaterialBinding shapes, so layout.$ still advertises the wrong WGSL resource for admitted input. Independently reproduced with passing exact assertions for the incorrect array/comparison-only types, failing assertions for the required unions, and runtime outputs texture_2d/filtering. Existing new tests cover required union-valued options, not optional properties. Preserve the undefined/default case when extracting optional values.
